The final step of the CYK algorithm is to check if the start symbol 'S' is in P[1][n]. In this case, P[1][7] is empty. Since the set of non-terminals that can generate the entire string is empty (and thus does not contain the start symbol 'S'), the string cannot be generated by the grammar.

